@startuml time_sync_sequence
title NTP four-timestamp Time Synchronization — BC <-> RT (sub-address 1, SystemHandler)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 30

participant "Bus Controller\n(BC host)" as BC
participant "Remote Terminal\n(RT firmware)" as RT

note over BC, RT
  Two commands target **sub-address 1** (SystemHandler).
  Command payload format: [ opcode(1) | units(1) | value(4) ] = 6 bytes.
  ""units"" is the negative power of ten of the time unit (ms = 3).
  All values are little-endian on the wire.
end note

== Step 1 — SYNC_PROBE (opcode 0x06) ==

BC -> BC : T1 = clock.now_ms()
BC -> RT : CMD  sub=1  [ 0x06 | units | T1 (LE) ]\n6-byte command payload
note right of RT
  RT captures **T2** = clock.now_ms() on receipt,
  then **T3** = clock.now_ms() just before replying
  (T3 - T2 is the RT's own handling time)
end note
RT -> BC : RESP  sub=1  [ T2 | T3 (LE) ]\n8-byte response payload
BC -> BC : decode T2, T3 from response\nT4 = clock.now_ms()

== Step 2 — SYNC_FINAL (opcode 0x07) ==

note over BC
  BC sends T4 so the RT can complete
  all four timestamps on its side.
end note
BC -> RT : CMD  sub=1  [ 0x07 | units | T4 (LE) ]\n6-byte command payload

note over RT
  RT computes via compute_sync_fixed(T1, T2, T3, T4):
  path_delay = ((T4 - T1) - (T3 - T2)) / 2   (one-way, RTT/2)
  offset     = ((T1 - T2) + (T4 - T3)) / 2
  (offset is BC - RT; positive when BC clock leads)

  **RT-side discipline:**
  push (offset, path_delay) into the 8-deep min-delay
  ClockFilter; the lowest-delay sample of the recent
  window feeds the least-squares OffsetSmoother, which
  recovers the disciplined offset and the clock skew.
  Serializes the SELECTED (min-delay) path delay and the
  disciplined offset as four LE words (16 bytes).
end note

RT -> BC : RESP  sub=1  16-byte fixed-point result\n[ path_delay_whole | path_delay_frac | offset_whole | offset_frac ]

note over BC
  **Fixed-point encoding (per word)**
  ""path_delay_whole"" — uint32, whole units (>= 0)
  ""path_delay_frac""  — uint32, thousandths of a unit (0..999)
  ""offset_whole""     — int32,  whole units (signed, BC - RT)
  ""offset_frac""      — int32,  thousandths (-999..999, sign matches whole)
  e.g. -1.5 ms encodes as { whole=-1, frac=-500 }

  Offset bytes (8..15) carry the **disciplined** value the RT
  already applied to its clock — BC stores it directly,
  no further filtering needed.

  Getters available after at least one successful exchange:
  ""has_sync()"" / ""clock_offset_units()"" / ""path_delay_units()"" / ""sync_units()""
end note

@enduml
